# Git — manual only

- Do NOT run `git commit`, `git push`, `git tag`, or change remotes unless the user explicitly asks in the current message.
- Do NOT use `git commit --amend`, `git reset`, or force-push unless explicitly requested.
- Staging (`git add`) is allowed only when the user asks to prepare a commit; otherwise leave changes unstaged.
- If preservation or “save state” is needed, report `git status` / diff and tell the user what to run; do not commit for them.
